WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.414 --> 00:00:16.464
"Aren't ever going to zap again?"

2
00:00:16.944 --> 00:00:17.605
Zann thought.

3
00:00:18.265 --> 00:00:20.747
Krub and the goon had slept late that morning.

4
00:00:21.448 --> 00:00:25.912
After a leisurely breakfast, Krub had zapped them all to this grassy hillside.

5
00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:30.496
Since then Krub and the goon had been drinking from their flasks again.

6
00:00:31.324 --> 00:00:33.146
Zann just wanted to get going.

7
00:00:33.986 --> 00:00:39.071
Finally Krub took an extra-long swig from his flask and let out a loud burp.

8
00:00:40.952 --> 00:00:43.415
"Let's move on," he said.

9
00:00:43.435 --> 00:00:45.096
"Get over here, kid."

10
00:00:45.937 --> 00:00:46.958
Zann shuffled over.

11
00:00:47.498 --> 00:00:48.699
The two men grabbed him.

12
00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.902
Krub rubbed his free hand against his leg.

13
00:00:51.922 --> 00:00:57.226
"Zap!" They landed in a swampy area.

14
00:00:57.727 --> 00:01:01.285
The air was humid, and streams and puddles were everywhere.

15
00:01:01.305 --> 00:01:03.507
"We're almost there."

16
00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:07.089
The goon peered into the thick, dripping trees.

17
00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:09.850
"The mines are a short hike from here."

18
00:01:10.711 --> 00:01:12.172
He and Krub set off.

19
00:01:12.992 --> 00:01:17.315
Zann shuffled after them, but the shackles on his legs made it difficult to walk.

20
00:01:17.335 --> 00:01:18.835
"Hey, wait up!"

21
00:01:19.076 --> 00:01:19.516
he called.

22
00:01:20.716 --> 00:01:21.517
Krub frowned.

23
00:01:21.537 --> 00:01:23.018
"Oh, right."

24
00:01:23.878 --> 00:01:26.600
He snapped his fingers and muttered something under his breath.

25
00:01:27.276 --> 00:01:29.718
The shackles on Zann's legs disappeared.

26
00:01:30.999 --> 00:01:32.380
The goon looked impressed.

27
00:01:33.121 --> 00:01:34.482
"How'd you do that?"

28
00:01:35.603 --> 00:01:37.345
"Never mind," Krub said.

29
00:01:37.365 --> 00:01:38.465
"Let's go."

30
00:01:39.306 --> 00:01:41.888
Zann didn't need Krub to tell him what had happened.

31
00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:45.671
He guessed that Zira had put a password on her Shackle spell.

32
00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:50.656
That would allow anyone who knew the password to remove or replace the shackles.

33
00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:55.600
"Zira probably heard me and Perda telling Mellis about magical passwords," Zann thought.

34
00:01:56.424 --> 00:01:59.166
"I wish I'd heard the password Zira put on my shackles."

35
00:02:00.747 --> 00:02:03.509
He was sure Krub would put the shackles back on at night.

36
00:02:04.109 --> 00:02:05.831
He would listen more carefully then.

37
00:02:06.471 --> 00:02:09.533
They hiked through the swamp and then headed uphill.

38
00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:14.437
Finally they heard voices nearby.

39
00:02:14.457 --> 00:02:18.059
"It sounds as if others are here," the goon said.

40
00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:19.480
Krub nodded.

41
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.982
"Don't tell them about magic."

42
00:02:23.363 --> 00:02:24.884
They entered a large clearing.

43
00:02:25.776 --> 00:02:31.419
Several people were hurrying in and out of a cave, while others sorted through piles of rocks and

44
00:02:31.479 --> 00:02:35.341
dirt. "I found flint," a man called out.

45
00:02:35.362 --> 00:02:37.403
"Let's go back in for more!"

46
00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.544
"Flint?" Zann said.

47
00:02:39.564 --> 00:02:41.605
"Why are they so excited to find that?"

48
00:02:42.325 --> 00:02:44.146
Krub shot him a surprised look.

49
00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.168
"To make fire, of course.

50
00:02:46.608 --> 00:02:48.749
It's a lot faster than rubbing sticks together."

51
00:02:49.589 --> 00:02:51.651
"Why are we bothering with this, anyway?"

52
00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:53.752
The goon scratched his head.

53
00:02:54.616 --> 00:02:57.438
"Can't we just have Zira and Vilkor make fire now?"

54
00:02:58.179 --> 00:02:58.659
He shrugged.

55
00:02:58.679 --> 00:03:02.082
"We might even be able to do it ourselves if we really try."

56
00:03:03.303 --> 00:03:04.644
Krub looked intrigued.

57
00:03:04.664 --> 00:03:09.208
"Zira made magic sound too difficult for anyone except her.

58
00:03:10.329 --> 00:03:14.292
But I can transport us long distances and create food.

59
00:03:15.193 --> 00:03:17.255
How can making fire be that much harder?"

60
00:03:17.275 --> 00:03:18.756
"Let's try!"

61
00:03:18.776 --> 00:03:23.400
The goon rubbed his meaty hands together and then pointed at the ground.

62
00:03:24.044 --> 00:03:27.806
"Fire!" A wisp of smoke appeared briefly.

63
00:03:28.446 --> 00:03:29.646
Zann rolled his eyes.

64
00:03:30.227 --> 00:03:33.748
They were out of the swamp, but the ground here was still pretty moist.

65
00:03:35.189 --> 00:03:36.189
Krub tried next.

66
00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.290
He created friction and then held out his hand.

67
00:03:40.231 --> 00:03:43.692
"Fire!" A small fireball appeared in his hand.

68
00:03:44.232 --> 00:03:46.693
Krub's eyes widened, and his jaw dropped.

69
00:03:47.153 --> 00:03:50.755
But as the fireball got a little larger, he quickly tossed it away.

70
00:03:50.775 --> 00:03:53.216
"Ouch!" He shook his hand.

71
00:03:53.772 --> 00:03:54.632
"It burned me!"

72
00:03:55.633 --> 00:03:57.253
Zann tried not to laugh.

73
00:03:57.934 --> 00:04:00.875
Meanwhile the men's shouts were attracting attention.

74
00:04:01.595 --> 00:04:05.497
Several miners came over when the goon set a small shrub on fire.

75
00:04:05.517 --> 00:04:07.318
"What's going on?"

76
00:04:07.618 --> 00:04:08.378
a miner asked.

77
00:04:08.398 --> 00:04:09.658
"Did you do that?"

78
00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:12.740
The goon tried to stamp out the burning bush.

79
00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.941
"None of your business!"

80
00:04:14.961 --> 00:04:20.303
"Does this have something to do with the way plants are growing and the land is thriving?"

81
00:04:20.643 --> 00:04:21.383
a woman asked.

82
00:04:22.043 --> 00:04:23.124
Another miner nodded.

83
00:04:23.592 --> 00:04:25.294
"It's strange but also wonderful!

84
00:04:26.014 --> 00:04:28.236
My orchard was barren until a few days ago.

85
00:04:28.957 --> 00:04:31.559
Now I have more fruit than my family can eat!"

86
00:04:32.299 --> 00:04:33.060
"It's magic!"

87
00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.581
the goon blurted out.

88
00:04:35.162 --> 00:04:37.584
He went on to tell the miners everything.

89
00:04:38.705 --> 00:04:40.086
Krub looked angry at first.

90
00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:44.489
But when the miners stared at him in awe, he couldn't resist showing off.

91
00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.491
"I can do magic too!"

92
00:04:47.032 --> 00:04:50.454
He quickly rubbed a hand on his side, and then waved his arms.

93
00:04:50.474 --> 00:04:52.096
"Drink for everyone!"

94
00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:54.321
Several flasks appeared.

95
00:04:54.942 --> 00:04:57.985
The miners grabbed them eagerly, tasting the contents.

96
00:04:58.005 --> 00:04:59.866
"This is a miracle!"

97
00:05:00.287 --> 00:05:00.787
one cried.

98
00:05:00.807 --> 00:05:02.508
"Will you show us how to do it?"

99
00:05:03.329 --> 00:05:05.011
"No." Krub frowned.

100
00:05:05.031 --> 00:05:07.933
"And don't try to do magic on your own.

101
00:05:08.454 --> 00:05:11.837
It's forbidden by the owner of the well from which the magic came!"

102
00:05:13.158 --> 00:05:15.460
The miners didn't look intimidated by the warning.

103
00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:20.144
Already some were waving their hands around, trying to imitate what Krub had done.

104
00:05:20.952 --> 00:05:23.833
"They didn't notice Krub creating friction," Zann thought.

105
00:05:23.853 --> 00:05:26.835
"They won't be able to do magic until they figure that out."

106
00:05:27.435 --> 00:05:29.276
He was tempted to shout out the truth.

107
00:05:29.816 --> 00:05:32.397
After all, magic should belong to everyone.

108
00:05:33.058 --> 00:05:35.939
But then he glanced down at his shackled hands.

109
00:05:36.499 --> 00:05:40.081
He needed to get that password before he did anything else.

110
00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:43.622
Maybe it would release Perda and Mellis too.

111
00:05:44.623 --> 00:05:46.644
To distract himself, he looked around.

112
00:05:47.372 --> 00:05:50.955
This part of Terrica reminded him of the hills near Swamp Bottom.

113
00:05:52.576 --> 00:05:56.058
That made him miss Magica more than ever—and Zing.

114
00:05:56.078 --> 00:06:01.222
"Ow!" he blurted out as an insect landed on his arm and gave him a painful bite.

115
00:06:01.762 --> 00:06:04.224
He tried to swat it, but the shackles stopped him.

116
00:06:04.244 --> 00:06:07.646
"I'm glad we don't have those nasty bugs in Magica," he thought.

117
00:06:08.307 --> 00:06:10.468
"Still, a lot of the trees and stuff look so familiar.

118
00:06:11.049 --> 00:06:12.010
I wish Darb were here.

119
00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:15.072
He'd notice all the little differences between here and home."

120
00:06:16.264 --> 00:06:17.585
The goon grabbed his arm.

121
00:06:17.605 --> 00:06:19.386
"Time to get to work."

122
00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:22.509
Zann had no choice but to stumble after him.

123
00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:29.994
As the goon dragged him past a crooked tree surrounded by a tangle of brush, Zann noticed something

124
00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:31.355
in the clearing beyond.

125
00:06:31.755 --> 00:06:34.958
Was it a cloud of those biting insects coming for him?

126
00:06:35.558 --> 00:06:37.599
Then he blinked in surprise.

127
00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.201
No, it wasn't insects.

128
00:06:41.022 --> 00:06:42.463
It was a shimmer in the air.

129
00:06:43.143 --> 00:06:45.095
Could it be a wormhole?
